# Riverchurn Monument: "{1}, {T}: Any number of target players each mill two cards." Any number is none too (CR 115.1d,
# 601.2c): on turn 1 Bot1 activates it with the {C} left over from casting it and chooses no player - the Monument is
# tapped and nobody mills. On turn 3 Bot1 targets Bot2 alone, whose library holds one card: the same player can't be
# chosen twice for one "target" (CR 115.3), so Bot2 named twice is refused, and Bot2 mills the one card there is
# (CR 701.17b: as many as possible) without losing - milling is not drawing (CR 704.5b). Bot1 mills nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Mox Sapphire
Riverchurn Monument
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x7
Swamp
Plains

